1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,185
Successful product launch includes a successful go-to-market strategy.

2
00:00:04,185 --> 00:00:08,355
Your marketing team can't create one without you or if they do,

3
00:00:08,355 --> 00:00:12,100
it might not reflect the protocols the way you would envision them.

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:16,260
So what do we need for a great product marketing strategy?

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,965
Who creates this strategy in the first place?

6
00:00:18,965 --> 00:00:20,625
As I said earlier,

7
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:25,530
a good go-to-market strategy is a product of product and marketing collaboration.

8
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:28,465
Neither side should be doing it alone,

9
00:00:28,465 --> 00:00:31,080
unless of course you are a small company,

10
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,235
there you and a product manager are doing everything.

11
00:00:34,235 --> 00:00:37,525
But what does that mean you're doing it in collaboration?

12
00:00:37,525 --> 00:00:39,905
It goes back to our previous point.

13
00:00:39,905 --> 00:00:43,370
Start by communicating as early as possible in the process.

14
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:45,850
Let marketing be a full partner.

15
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,470
It is a good idea to have a document where

16
00:00:48,470 --> 00:00:51,110
you outline what are your product is all about.

17
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,760
If it has a regular release,

18
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,970
the one where you just add a new feature,

19
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:58,220
it is still a good idea to keep your marketing informed.

20
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,735
In a lot of cases,

21
00:00:59,735 --> 00:01:02,135
there is still work around new features,

22
00:01:02,135 --> 00:01:06,865
even if it is not a full scale go-to-market strategy or marketing plan.

23
00:01:06,865 --> 00:01:09,470
It is a good practice to have frequent meetings with

24
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:12,425
your marketing team to keep them in a loop.

25
00:01:12,425 --> 00:01:14,645
When you are going for a big launch,

26
00:01:14,645 --> 00:01:17,150
there is a lot of preparation that might be needed.

27
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:19,220
Do we want to create a social media buzz?

28
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:22,040
Professional bloggers, or maybe it is

29
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:25,025
an enterprise product there need to have a special event.

30
00:01:25,025 --> 00:01:27,385
The marketing team is there to help.

31
00:01:27,385 --> 00:01:29,445
You should outline your product,

32
00:01:29,445 --> 00:01:31,810
and together have your marketing team,

33
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:36,650
have multiple ideas on how to achieve the best exposure for your product.

34
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:38,720
Once you agree on the plan,

35
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,160
make sure to follow up with

36
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:43,745
your marketing team to see that as your launch is approaching,

37
00:01:43,745 --> 00:01:46,440
there are no last minute delays.

